Seasonality Analysis
Objective
- The seasonality analysis identifies recurring patterns in sales across time and evaluates the contribution of holiday periods.
Findings
- July and Q3 were among the strongest sales periods in the historical data.
- Holiday-period sales contributed approximately 7.5% of total revenue.
- Sales patterns demonstrate recurring temporal variation that should be incorporated into operational planning.
Interpretation
- Seasonality provides useful context for forecasting and planning because demand should not be treated as constant throughout the year.
Peak periods can affect:
- Inventory requirements
- Staffing requirements
- Replenishment
- Logistics capacity
- Promotional timing
